  "critical": false,
  "description": "Unpowered aerostats using heated air for lift. A fabric envelope traps warm air (typically 100-120°C above ambient), producing net buoyancy through density difference. Controlled by varying burner output for altitude; lateral movement relies on wind currents at different altitudes. The simplest flying machine, achievable with woven fabric and a propane or wood-fueled heat source.",
